    detail: "From the OECD's own data, Israeli current health expenditure was 7.089 percent of GDP in 2024, 39th of 50 reporting economies, against Germany 12.2 percent, France 11.3, the United Kingdom 11.1 and Japan 10.3. The 2023 financing mix was government and compulsory schemes 65.24 percent, voluntary schemes 12.83 percent and household out-of-pocket 20.49 percent. Two cautions. This is current expenditure and excludes capital formation, so it is not the same series as the Israeli Central Bureau of Statistics national health expenditure figure, which uses a different definition and gives a higher share; the two must not be mixed, and the CBS series could not be retrieved. And no OECD average is published from that dataflow, so none is quoted here.",
